WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.453
Architecture models organize ICS functions so teams can discuss dependencies, trust boundaries, and required communication.

00:00:07.453 --> 00:00:13.550
At the field level, sensors and actuators interact with the physical process.

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:18.293
The control level contains PLCs, RTUs, and other controllers.

00:00:18.293 --> 00:00:22.584
Supervisory systems provide operator views and higher-level coordination.

00:00:22.584 --> 00:00:30.940
Above direct supervision, operations systems may include historians, application servers, engineering services, production management, and site administration.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:38.393
Enterprise systems consume selected information and provide services such as identity, business planning, or support.

00:00:38.393 --> 00:00:44.039
These connections are useful, but they must be explicit and controlled.

00:00:44.039 --> 00:00:50.137
The Purdue model is a common reference for describing these functional layers.

00:00:50.137 --> 00:00:58.041
It can help identify how a connection crosses from enterprise activity toward site operations and control.

00:00:58.041 --> 00:01:08.204
It is not a perfect map of every modern environment, and it should not replace a site-specific architecture or data-flow analysis.

00:01:08.204 --> 00:01:13.850
An industrial DMZ is commonly placed between enterprise and industrial operations.

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:22.658
It can host intermediary services such as jump systems, remote-access brokers, update staging, file transfer, or historian replication.

00:01:22.658 --> 00:01:30.111
The objective is to avoid broad, direct connections while creating monitored points for necessary exchange.

00:01:30.111 --> 00:01:34.402
Segmentation groups assets by function, criticality, and trust.

00:01:34.402 --> 00:01:38.693
Controlled conduits permit only required communication between zones.

00:01:38.693 --> 00:01:49.307
Good design also accounts for redundancy, failover, management access, vendor support, safety systems, and what happens when a boundary device is unavailable.

00:01:49.307 --> 00:01:52.695
Architecture is a living operational record.

00:01:52.695 --> 00:02:01.503
Validate diagrams against observed traffic and engineering knowledge, document serial and wireless paths, assign owners, and update changes.

00:02:01.503 --> 00:02:13.021
A useful model helps teams predict consequence, place controls, investigate movement, and coordinate recovery without assuming that every site follows the same layered pattern.
